   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-01-30">January 30, 1942</date></dateline>
               <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr. Paul Tillich</rs><lb/>
               Union Theological Seminary<lb/><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York, New York</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                  Tillich</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>Enclosed is a copy of a letter <note type="ea">liegt nicht vor</note> I have just
               sent to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4253" type="person">Mr. Kenneth Leslie</rs>.</p>
            <p>May I congratulate you personally on your brochure which I believe to be prophetic.</p>
            <p>Already, it has inspired me to write two editorials, and I am now contemplating a
               third.</p>
            
            <closer>
               <salute>Sincerely yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4252" type="person"
                  ><hi rend="hand">Sol Silverman</hi>Sol Silverman Publisher</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
